cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ArabicFinBench, please cite it as below, and also cite the upstream ExtractBench harness."
title: "ArabicFinBench: an evaluation benchmark for Arabic financial-document understanding"
abstract: >-
  ArabicFinBench evaluates Arabic financial-document understanding along three
  separately reported axes - Parse, Extract, and Finance (P/E/F) - which are
  never combined into a single score. It is a fork of the ExtractBench harness.
  This release is a methodology preview: ten systems scored on a five-document
  corpus that is not yet redistributable, with the Parse and Finance axes
  reported. It is not a leaderboard and its rankings are not significance-tested.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Firas013/ArabicFinBench"
url: "https://github.com/Firas013/ArabicFinBench"
keywords:
  - arabic
  - finance
  - benchmark
  - document-understanding
  - information-extraction
authors:
  # UNFILLED. Citation metadata must not be guessed on an author's behalf, so
  # these stay bracketed until the author fills them in. A release should not be
  # tagged while this block still reads <FAMILY-NAME>.
  - family-names: "<FAMILY-NAME>"
    given-names: "<GIVEN-NAME>"
    affiliation: "<AFFILIATION>"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
references:
